module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.FunctorToTypes
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FibreDegreeStratification
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Glueing.FppfCovering
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ModificationsAtClosedPoints
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ZariskiCoveringPoints

/-!
# The étale covering of a space by the chosen neighborhoods and the complement of the points

Let `X` be a decent algebraic space over a scheme `S`, let `x₁, …, xₙ ∈ |X|` be pairwise
distinct closed points and let `(Uᵢ, uᵢ) → (X, xᵢ)` be the chosen elementary étale
neighborhoods of Stacks 0BH9. The family

`{X ∖ {x₁, …, xₙ} ⟶ X} ∪ {Uᵢ ⟶ X}`

is an étale covering of `X`: every member is étale, and a point of `X` is either not one of the
chosen points, or it is `xᵢ` and so the image of `uᵢ`. This is the covering along which the
proof of Stacks 0BHB glues a modification of `X` out of the modifications of the `Uᵢ` given by
an object of the target of the functor of Stacks 0BHA.

## Main definitions

All names below are in the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ClosedPointNeighborhoods`.

* `coverObj` and `coverHom` are the members of that covering and their morphisms to `X`.

## Main results

* `sheafify_iSup_range_coverHom_eq_top`: the subfunctor of `X` generated by the images of the
  covering sheafifies to the whole of `X`.
* `sheafify_iSup_range_pullback_fst_coverHom_eq_top`: the same after an arbitrary base change
  `P ⟶ X`.

## Implementation notes

Being a covering is recorded as the sheafification of the subfunctor generated by the images
being everything, which is the form a descent argument consumes: a section of `X` over a test
object restricts, along the arrows of a covering sieve, into the image of one member. Local
surjectivity of the morphism out of the *coproduct* of the members would say the same thing only
after the same unwinding, since a section of a coproduct of presheaves carries no information
about the members beyond the one it comes from.

The members are indexed by `Option (Fin n)`, the complement being the `none` member; the join of
a family of subfunctors accepts any index type. A Zariski covering in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsZariskiCover` must be indexed by a type of the working universe, so
the intermediate covering below is indexed by `ULift.{u} (Option (Fin n))`.

The covering is étale and not Zariski, so the point criterion of Stacks 03BZ does not apply to
it directly. Each `Uᵢ ⟶ X` is replaced by the open subspace `Iᵢ ⊆ X` it sweeps out, which is
Stacks 06NF in the form `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isOpenSubspace_etaleImage`: that
produces `Iᵢ` with the same point set as the image of `Uᵢ`, together with a surjective étale
morphism `Uᵢ ⟶ Iᵢ` over `X`. The complement together with the `Iᵢ` is then a Zariski covering
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZariskiCover_iff_iUnion_points`, and the surjective étale
morphisms `Uᵢ ⟶ Iᵢ` are locally surjective, which refines the `Iᵢ` back to the `Uᵢ` at the cost
of one further sheafification. That second sheafification is absorbed by
`CategoryTheory.Subfunctor.sheafify_le`, the ambient presheaf being a sheaf because `X` is an
algebraic space.

The base-changed statement is deduced from the first by naming sections with the Yoneda lemma: a
section of `P` whose image in `X` lifts to a member `a` of the covering lifts to
`P ×_X (covering member a)`, the lift being `CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.lift` of the two
morphisms out of the representable presheaf named by the two sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BHB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BHB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BH9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BH9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

namespace ClosedPointNeighborhoods

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} {n : ℕ}
  (D : ClosedPointNeighborhoods B S hS n)

/-- The members of the étale covering of `X` by the open complement of the chosen points and
the chosen neighborhoods. -/
def coverObj : Option (Fin n) → ((BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u)
  | none => D.openAwayFromPoints.toFunctor
  | some i => (D.neighborhoodSpace i).obj

/-- The morphisms of that covering. -/
def coverHom : ∀ a, D.coverObj a ⟶ D.space.obj
  | none => D.openAwayFromPoints.ι
  | some i => (D.toSpaceHom i).hom

/-- **The chosen neighborhoods and the complement of the chosen points cover `X`.** The
subfunctor of `X` generated by the images of the covering sheafifies to the whole of `X`: every
section of `X` over a test object restricts, along the arrows of a covering sieve, into the image
of the complement or of one of the neighborhoods. -/
theorem sheafify_iSup_range_coverHom_eq_top :
    (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).sheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  have hsheaf : Presieve.IsSheaf (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) D.space.obj :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 D.space.property.isSheaf
  -- the open subspace swept out by each neighborhood, with its surjective étale chart
  choose I ψ hIopen hψι hψsurj hψetale hIpoints using fun i : Fin n ↦
    exists_isOpenSubspace_etaleImage B S hS D.space.property (D.neighborhood i).scheme
      (D.toSpaceHom i).hom
      (presheaf_etale_of_isEtale B S hS (D.neighborhood i).etale_toSpace)
  obtain ⟨pieces, hnone, hsome⟩ :
      ∃ pieces : ULift.{u} (Option (Fin n)) → Subfunctor D.space.obj,
        pieces (ULift.up none) = D.openAwayFromPoints ∧
          ∀ i, pieces (ULift.up (some i)) = I i :=
    ⟨fun a ↦ a.down.elim D.openAwayFromPoints I, rfl, fun _ ↦ rfl⟩
  -- the complement and those open subspaces form a Zariski covering of `X`
  have hopen : ∀ a, IsOpenSubspace B S hS (pieces a) := by
    rintro ⟨a⟩
    cases a with
    | none => rw [hnone]; exact D.isOpenSubspace_openAwayFromPoints
    | some i => rw [hsome i]; exact hIopen i
  have hcover : (⋃ a, Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (pieces a).toFunctor (pieces a).ι)) =
      Set.univ := by
    refine Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun x ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ?_
    by_cases hx : x ∈ Set.range D.point
    · obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
      refine ⟨ULift.up (some i), ?_⟩
      rw [hsome i, hIpoints i]
      exact ⟨D.neighborhoodPoint i, (D.neighborhood i).map_point⟩
    · refine ⟨ULift.up none, ?_⟩
      rwa [hnone, D.range_pointsMap_ι_openAwayFromPoints]
  have hls : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)
      (Sigma.desc fun a ↦ (pieces a).ι) :=
    ((isZariskiCover_iff_iUnion_points B S hS D.space.obj D.space.property _ pieces hopen).mpr
      hcover).2
  -- a section of the coproduct of the members comes from a member
  have hrange : Subfunctor.range (Sigma.desc fun a ↦ (pieces a).ι) ≤ ⨆ a, pieces a := by
    intro T x hx
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : ∃ t, (Sigma.desc fun a ↦ (pieces a).ι).app T t = x := hx
    obtain ⟨⟨a⟩, s, rfl⟩ := FunctorToTypes.jointly_surjective'
      (Discrete.functor fun a ↦ (pieces a).toFunctor) T t
    have hcomp : (Sigma.desc fun a ↦ (pieces a).ι).app T
        ((Sigma.ι (fun a ↦ (pieces a).toFunctor) a).app T s) = (pieces a).ι.app T s := by
      rw [← NatTrans.comp_app_apply, Sigma.ι_desc]
    rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj, ← ht, hcomp]
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨a, s.2⟩
  -- each member of the Zariski covering lies locally in the image of the étale covering
  have hG : ∀ a, pieces a ≤
      (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).sheafify (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) := by
    rintro ⟨a⟩
    cases a with
    | none =>
        rw [hnone]
        exact (le_of_eq_of_le (Subfunctor.range_ι D.openAwayFromPoints).symm
          (le_iSup (fun a ↦ Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)) none)).trans
          ((⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).le_sheafify _)
    | some i =>
        rw [hsome i]
        intro T p hp
        have hlsψ : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) (ψ i) :=
          isLocallySurjective_of_surjective_etale B S hS (ψ i) (hψsurj i) (hψetale i)
        refine (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).superset_covering ?_
          (hlsψ.imageSieve_mem (⟨p, hp⟩ : (I i).toFunctor.obj T))
        rintro Z h ⟨t, ht⟩
        change D.space.obj.map h.op p ∈ (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).obj (op Z)
        rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj]
        refine Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨some i, t, ?_⟩
        change (D.toSpaceHom i).hom.app (op Z) t = D.space.obj.map h.op p
        rw [← hψι i]
        exact congrArg ((I i).ι.app (op Z)) ht
  exact top_le_iff.1 (le_of_eq_of_le
    ((Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_range_sheafify_eq_top' _ _).1 hls).symm
    (Subfunctor.sheafify_le _ _ (hrange.trans (iSup_le hG)) hsheaf
      (Subfunctor.sheafify_isSheaf _ hsheaf)))

/-- **The covering of `X` stays a covering after an arbitrary base change.** For every morphism
`g : P ⟶ X` of presheaves on the big fppf site over `S`, the subfunctor of `P` generated by the
images of the first projections of the fibre products `P ×_X (covering member)` sheafifies to the
whole of `P`. -/
theorem sheafify_iSup_range_pullback_fst_coverHom_eq_top
    {P : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (g : P ⟶ D.space.obj) :
    (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.fst g (D.coverHom a))).sheafify
      (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS) = ⊤ := by
  refine top_le_iff.1 ?_
  intro T p _
  have hcov : (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).sieveOfSection (g.app T p) ∈
      BigFppfOver.topology B S hS T.unop := by
    change g.app T p ∈ ((⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).sheafify
      (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)).obj T
    rw [D.sheafify_iSup_range_coverHom_eq_top]; trivial
  refine (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS).superset_covering ?_ hcov
  intro Z h hh
  have hh' : D.space.obj.map h.op (g.app T p) ∈
      (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (D.coverHom a)).obj (op Z) := hh
  rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj] at hh'
  obtain ⟨a, c, hc⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 hh'
  have hw : yonedaEquiv.symm (P.map h.op p) ≫ g =
      yonedaEquiv.symm c ≫ D.coverHom a := by
    rw [yonedaEquiv_symm_naturality_right, yonedaEquiv_symm_naturality_right, hc,
      NatTrans.naturality_apply]
  change P.map h.op p ∈ (⨆ a, Subfunctor.range (pullback.fst g (D.coverHom a))).obj (op Z)
  rw [Subfunctor.iSup_obj]
  refine Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨a, yonedaEquiv (pullback.lift _ _ hw), ?_⟩
  rw [← yonedaEquiv_comp, pullback.lift_fst, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

end ClosedPointNeighborhoods

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
